Warped clips as Segno plays them (docs/design/audio-editor.md §15, ADR 0063).

A clip that follows the tempo plays past its edges as an unwarped one does (EngineBehaviour's
getAudioClipExtension, for crossfades): its beat range widened, its offset in beats moved to match.
And a clip can ask to follow the tempo by resampling rather than stretching (a "resample" property
on its state, with no transposition): speed and pitch move together, Segno's Repitch, and a warped
clip at its own tempo reads its file untouched, with no stretcher to run.

diff '--color=auto' -ru a/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.cpp b/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.cpp
